From ac4b6a119f6b6399fc0e0247a2fe99713e677bda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunW3 <0176778602@naver.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 16:26:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/22] b200: bump NCCL collective timeout to 1h for
 shared-host tolerance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The default NCCL collective timeout is 10 min. On a shared host under
load (we observed avg 700+), a single all_reduce can stall for tens
of minutes while another job hogs the PCIe/disk/CPU. That blew up our
training at step ~79433:

  [rank0]:[F525 15:47:58 ProcessGroupNCCL.cpp:1554] [...] Terminating
   the process after attempting to dump debug info, due to collective
   timeout or exception.

  Last enqueued NCCL work: 4798306, last completed NCCL work: 4798306

Bumping init_process_group(timeout=timedelta(hours=1)) lets the
training survive the noisy-neighbour periods. Lost ~1500 steps from
ckpt 78000 → 79433; resume re-traverses them automatically.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lingua/distributed.py | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lingua/distributed.py b/lingua/distributed.py
index 81295a2..1ea7b0c 100644
--- a/lingua/distributed.py
+++ b/lingua/distributed.py
@@ -278,7 +278,13 @@ def setup_torch_distributed(dist_args):
     )
     if torch.cuda.device_count() > 1:
         torch.cuda.set_device(local_rank)
-    torch.distributed.init_process_group(init_method="env://", backend="nccl")
+    # Default NCCL collective timeout is 10 min — too short for shared-host runs where
+    # transient load spikes can stall a single collective for tens of minutes. Bump to 1h
+    # so the training survives noisy neighbours.
+    from datetime import timedelta
+    torch.distributed.init_process_group(
+        init_method="env://", backend="nccl", timeout=timedelta(hours=1)
+    )
     torch.autograd.set_detect_anomaly(dist_args.detect_anomaly)
 
 
